The Chief Officer approved Landfall's new palette with notes on the first call, and the outcome is recorded under **Palette distinctness** in `landfall/design/choices.md`. The Developer can start copying the palette now.

**What changed: teal acts, navy speaks.** Overwing puts navy on every call to action and on a dark navy wall, with teal as a thin line. Landfall now does the opposite:

| Role | Old | New | Overwing |
|---|---|---|---|
| Buttons and selections (Search, Done, Sign in, compact search, picked dates, checked options) | navy | lagoon teal #14A08B with an ink label (5.3:1) | navy |
| Navy | #0F2747, on every call to action | indigo #1B2A6E, for words and the destination cards only, never a button, no navy wall | #0D2B4C, #0B2341 |
| Teal shade | #0A7C78 | about twice as light and greener than Overwing's | #086F76 |
| Bright teal | #4FD1C1 | #5FE3C2, used only on navy and the photo | #6FD6CE |
| Ink | #0B1830 | #121839 | #0B1B2E |
| Tint | #EAF2F4 | #EDF9F6 | #E6F0F2 |

- **Harbour gold is unchanged.** Its Search button still shows #173B4F.
- **Contrast:**
  - Every text pair is 4.5:1 or better.
  - Text on all three hero photos holds 4.9:1 or better at 1440 and 390.
  - Teal is never used as text on white, because it only reaches 3.3:1 there.
- **Focus ring fix:** the bright focus ring fell to 1.1:1 on Lisbon's white buildings at 390. The old palette had the same fault. I added a dark halo behind focus rings on the photo, and the ring now sits at about 8:1.
- **Files:** besides `tokens.css` and `index.html`, I had to edit `prototype/assets/global.css`. That is where the prototype's copy of the tokens and its button rules live.
- **Screenshots:** the hero at 1440 and 390, the open dates panel, the destination cards, the focus ring, and Harbour for comparison. They are in `landfall/design/screens/palette-distinctness/`.

**Decisions for you:**
1. **Teal buttons break your V6 default (navy on light backgrounds), and Kasa uses navy too.** Your instruction to use different roles comes first in the art-direct order, so I went with teal. It's marked provisional in `choices.md` until you confirm.
2. **The Chief Officer thinks #1B2A6E looks royal blue rather than deep navy on the destination cards.** I kept the approved value so the Developer copies one settled set. If you agree, #16225A is the same hue but darker, already measured, and a one-value swap.

**What I couldn't check:**
- I never saw Overwing's screens, only the values you gave me.
- I didn't check hover states on screen, real phones, Safari, Firefox, widths between 641 and 1024, or reduced motion.
- The Chief Officer also spotted a small stray mark and a possibly hidden heading under the pinned search bar. That's layout, not palette, and it was there before this change, so I left it for the Developer.

**Process slip:** I rewrote the palette blocks with a small Python script instead of the edit tool. It saved the two files with different line endings, so I put Windows line endings back to match the folder's other files. Checking against git needs your approval, so please glance at the diff for those two files.

The run is logged in `review-log.md`, and the preview server I started is stopped.

This is a good checkpoint. Suggested commit message: `Landfall: own navy and teal palette (teal fills actions, indigo navy), Palette distinctness approved`
